MaxxOS AOSP 
==============

Getting Started
---------------

To get started with Android, you'll need to get
familiar with [Git and Repo](http://source.android.com/source/using-repo.html).

To initialize your local repository using the MaxxOS trees, use a command like this:

```bash
repo init -u https://github.com/MaxxOS-AOSP/manifest.git -b staging --git-lfs
```
Then to sync up:
```bash
repo sync -j$(nproc --all) --no-tags --no-clone-bundle --current-branch
```

### Build Configuration Flags (Optional)
If you want to include Google Apps (GApps) directly in your build, make sure to put flag in maxx_device.mk flag before starting the compilation:

```bash
TARGET_BUILD_GAPPS := true
```
# If you want to enable blur :

```bash
 TARGET_ENABLE_BLUR := true
```

### Version / About-phone banner flags (Optional)

The Settings → About phone header reads these `ro.maxx.*` properties. Chipset, phone number, etc. are auto-detected; the ROM-identity ones come from `vendor/yaap/config/version.mk` and can be overridden in the device makefile (`device.mk` / `yaap_device.mk`):

```make
# device/<brand>/<device>/device.mk
MAXX_BUILDTYPE := OFFICIAL
MAXX_MAINTAINER := yourname
PRODUCT_SYSTEM_DEFAULT_PROPERTIES += \
    ro.maxx.maintainer=$(MAXX_MAINTAINER)
```

`MAXX_BUILDTYPE` controls the official/community badge (use `OFFICIAL`; default is `HOMEMADE`). Add `ro.maxx.maintainer=$(MAXX_MAINTAINER)` as above or via `vendor/yaap/config/version.mk`.

| Flag | Default | Sets |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `MAXX_BUILDTYPE` | `HOMEMADE` | `ro.maxx.buildtype` — controls the About phone official/community badge. Use `OFFICIAL` for official builds. |
| `MAXX_MAINTAINER` | *(none)* | Add `ro.maxx.maintainer=$(MAXX_MAINTAINER)` to version.mk and export this env var to show the maintainer name in About phone. |
| `MAXX_BUILD_VERSION` | `$(PLATFORM_VERSION)` | `ro.maxx.build.version` |
| `MAXX_VERSION` | version-buildtype-device-date | `ro.maxx.version` |
| `MAXX_BUILD` / `TARGET_PRODUCT` | lunch choice | `ro.maxx.device` |
| `BUILD_DATE` | date | `ro.maxx.build.date` |

Example:

```bash
export MAXX_MAINTAINER=yourname   # after adding ro.maxx.maintainer to vendor/yaap/config/version.mk
MAXX_BUILDTYPE=OFFICIAL m yaap
```



## Building the source
---------------

The source at MaxxOS AOSP is well configured for building.

```bash
source build/envsetup.sh
lunch yaap_device-user && m yaap
```
